freedreno: survive NULL BOs on draws, shaders and ringbuffers after GPU OOM

With a 32 MiB SweetGPU carve-out, once GPU memory is exhausted,
fd_resource_create() / realloc_bo() fails and leaves resources with
rsc->bo == NULL, or sub-allocations (bindless descriptor sets, LRZ
buffers, shader variant BOs, and command-stream ringbuffer BOs) fail to
allocate a BO. Subsequent draws or clears that bind those resources,
compile/upload shaders, or emit into a NULL ringbuffer BO crash
backboardd.

- freedreno_draw.c / freedreno_draw.h: add fd_oom_note_skip() (logs once
  via mesa_loge and sweet_drm_log on __APPLE__, and counts skips) and
  helper checks for NULL BOs on bound vertex/index/SO/indirect buffers,
  shader UBOs/SSBOs/images/sampler views, and framebuffer surfaces.
  Skip fd_draw_vbo(), fd_clear(), fd_clear_render_target(),
  fd_clear_depth_stencil(), and fd_launch_grid() when any bound
  resource has rsc->bo == NULL.
- freedreno_blitter.c: skip fd_blit() and fd_resource_copy_region() when
  src or dst resource has rsc->bo == NULL.
- ir3/ir3_gallium.c: in upload_shader_variant(), return early if
  fd_bo_new() returns NULL instead of calling fd_bo_mark_for_dump(NULL).
- a6xx/fd6_image.cc: in fd6_build_bindless_state(), return NULL if
  fd_bo_new() or fd_bo_map() fails instead of calling
  fd_bo_mark_for_dump(NULL).
- a6xx/fd6_draw.cc: skip fd6_draw_vbos() when a shader variant has
  bo == NULL, and in fd6_clear() guard subpass->lrz == NULL before
  calling fd_bo_ref().
- drm/freedreno_ringbuffer_sp.*: when fd_bo_new_ring() / fd_bo_map()
  fails, back the ringbuffer with a temporary CPU scratch buffer, guard
  NULL BO relocs/refs, mark the fd_submit_sp as OOM, and drop the
  incomplete submit before ioctl in fd_submit_sp_flush_execute() while
  still advancing the software fence.

Applies after 0001-0004. Mesa is MIT licensed; this patch is too.

